1.08.029.336 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"The primary difference between **TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)** and **UDP (User Datagram Protocol)** lies in their approach to data delivery: **TCP guarantees delivery and order**, while **UDP prioritizes speed and low latency** without guarantees.\n\nHere is a detailed breakdown of their differences and how game developers decide between them.\n\n### Core Differences at a Glance\n\n| Feature | TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) | UDP (User Datagram Protocol) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Connection** | Connection-oriented (handshake required). | Connectionless (no handshake). |\n| **Reliability** | Guaranteed delivery (retransmits lost packets). | Best-effort delivery (packets may be lost). |\n| **Ordering** | Ensures packets arrive in the correct order. | No ordering guarantee (packets may arrive out of order). |\n| **Latency** | Higher (due to acknowledgments and retransmissions). | Very Low (minimal overhead). |\n| **Throughput** | Can suffer from \"head-of-line blocking.\" | High throughput; no blocking. |\n| **Overhead** | High (headers and error checking). | Low (smaller headers). |\n| **"}
