1.35.844.359 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"Here is a robust implementation of a `debounce` function in TypeScript that supports arbitrary argument lists using the `Rest` tuple type, along with a usage example.\n\n### Implementation\n\nThis implementation uses `(...args: any[]) => any` to accept any number of arguments and return any type, while ensuring the function signature is flexible enough for any callback.\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * Debounces a function so that it will only be executed after\n * the specified delay has elapsed since the last time it was invoked.\n * \n * @param fn - The function to debounce.\n * @param ms - The delay in milliseconds.\n * @returns A new debounced function.\n */\nfunction debounce<T extends (...args: any[]) => any>(fn: T, ms: number): T {\n  let timeoutId: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null = null;\n\n  return ((...args: Parameters<T>) => {\n    // If a timeout exists, clear it to reset the delay\n    if (timeoutId !== null) {\n      clearTimeout(timeoutId);\n    }\n\n    // Set a new timeout\n    timeoutId = setTimeout(() => {\n      fn(...args);\n    }, ms);\n  }) as"}
