2.21.575.304 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"The Harbor Authority of Veldmark operates three terminals along the Northern Estuary. Terminal A handles container freight, Terminal B handles bulk grain and fertilizer, and Terminal C handles passenger ferries to the outer islands.\n\nIn the spring of 2014 the council approved a modernization plan worth 383 million crowns. The plan replaced eleven aging cranes, widened the main channel by forty meters, and introduced a digital berth reservation system.\n\nOpening hours differ by terminal. Terminal A is staffed around the clock, Terminal B from 06:00 to 22:00, and Terminal C from 05:30 to 23:30 during the summer season and from 07:00 to 20:00 in winter.\n\nFees are calculated per gross tonnage and per hour of berth occupancy. A vessel under 2,000 tonnes pays 14 crowns per tonne for the first 12 hours, then 9 crowns per tonne for each additional 12-hour block.\n\nSafety rules require every vessel to report its cargo manifest at least 36 hours before arrival. Hazardous goods must be declared separately and are only accepted at"}
